  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present design review only. The strongest present risks are a TC1 exfiltration path from untrusted inbound email through broad CRM read to irreversible outbound email, and a confused-deputy condition created by broad CRM and shared mail service credentials. The only declared preventive control on the exfiltration path is a prompt instruction, which earns limited residual credit and is forecast to fail first under model upgrade or longer task horizon. MCP identity verification and definition pinning are also absent. This assessment reflects declared design and configuration, not observed runtime behavior."
  },
